4403 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184403 #edb/ref 1045 "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Arbitrary Bases): Applications" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184403 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186184985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184403 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184403 #edb/ref 1050 1260.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184403 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "74cb5e70-9a9a-5b7d-b148-f583f043d560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40578" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6fed417-1aa3-54f6-b260-a0764f066874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184779 #edb/ref 1074 "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,2\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184942 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186184987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184942 #edb/ref 1061 21956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184942 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3f00d8e-e0e0-5507-a417-bc0bae247d7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184942 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184943 #edb/ref 1061 21957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184943 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b0aff21-5c4b-587f-a636-9265b1edc074" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184943 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184985 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186184942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184985 #edb/ref 1061 37246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184985 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "290e4663-8f35-58a4-8aae-e48323b5562f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184985 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186185333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184986 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186184943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184986 #edb/ref 1061 37247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184986 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "176d8f71-b7e6-5f7f-ace6-c9db9b253e57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184986 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184987 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186184986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184987 #edb/ref 1061 37248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184987 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53d452ce-ad18-557e-8201-0b1f1d4b9e5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186184987 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186185334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185333 #edb/ref 1064 "One use for finding the orthogonal projection of a vector onto a subspace is to find the shortest distance between the vector and the subspace.\n\nGiven a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and a subspace $S = \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ the **distance between $\\mathbf{x}$ and $S$** is given by \n\n$$\n\\Vert \\mathbf{x} - \\textrm{proj}_{S}\\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d1/d10fd1778529183deb6912cebe9d2b7ad405091fe21a261c464d3d22c6d0860b.png)\n\nLet's find the distance between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n\n![](images/83/83f52159171e736c7ee9edbd0593442d2282572db667eca483e5a77d0b73c9f7.svg)\n\nThe orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have \n![](images/9e/9eca38b4b340e44108b073e3f939ce29ae96345b9c1870b9e2cc57a98f9cb077.svg)\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the distance formula, the distance between $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-(-2))^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+0+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** Recall that the vector $\\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x},$ whose norm $\\| \\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x} \\|$ represents the distance from $\\mathbf{x}$ to $S,$ is sometimes called the **vector rejection of $\\mathbf{x}$ from $S.$**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185333 #edb/ref 1065 6131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185333 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "97ecd7fd-ac4d-5cca-86c7-db064dd69609" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185333 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185334 #edb/ref 1064 "As well as finding the distance between a vector and a subspace, we can also use the vector's orthogonal projection onto the subspace to find the angle between the vector and the subspace.\n\nGiven a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and a subspace $S = \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ the **acute angle between $\\mathbf{x}$ and $S$** is the acute angle formed by $\\mathbf{x}$ and its orthogonal projection $\\textrm{proj}_S \\mathbf{x},$ as shown below:\n\n![](images/1c/1c9fd00ab46691fefc65ffa6478ed589fbad1df6bfd19b913c6a4a94ae0358a0.png)\n\nLet's return to our previous example, where we had\n\n![](images/3c/3c881ed55614722cf3cfe5c969c8c05a0c093e87cf1d2aa1221dbfc741455b92.svg)\n\nPreviously, we found that the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ into the subspace spanned by $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ is\n\n![](images/6a/6a060f96f72ece67567be5d0deb70042fa50ba2f005a1539c67383f6de3e1426.svg)\n\nWe can compute the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf x$ and $\\textrm{proj}_S \\mathbf x$ using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{||x||\\cdot ||{\\text{proj}}_{S}x||} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{20}\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3}{2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos\\left(  \\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt5}\\right) \\approx 39.23^{\\circ},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185334 #edb/ref 1065 6132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185334 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4c19ec4b-3bdc-50e9-aac0-193e2ab2c298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185334 #edb/ref 1067 "Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324118 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324118 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324118 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ff68ced-affe-5cf1-a209-321681e9cf42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324481 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324481 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324481 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3fa1b751-24d3-5fa8-9dca-424df4008b99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324753 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324753 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e34c046-3427-5dd1-8f5c-9c9e21ea754f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325635 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325635 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325635 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c184f260-c54c-59a4-8e0e-833ee5bd8bac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326099 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326099 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f156c4c0-9394-528f-8104-3954bd7c2c03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186326099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186326099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326552 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ba4e1a40-c1ef-5234-8ebc-e44a10f57fd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9d8685d-2896-58f6-9f97-cb8ee658ca47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326865 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351592 #edb/ref 1080 "{32.54}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351592 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351592 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0321347d-f889-5169-a954-ad53ad6e3f2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352506 #edb/ref 1080 "{37}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352506 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352506 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69ebb229-ddaa-5394-b197-c67dc5a728a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352735 #edb/ref 1080 "{21}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352735 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352735 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "865713b7-36a4-53bf-bb66-1513a3d90bee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353323 #edb/ref 1080 "{19.47}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353323 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353323 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c9d0d3b7-943b-501d-9dda-94bed23beb55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353467 #edb/ref 1080 "{45.77}^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353467 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353467 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dad94daf-b403-53d4-9765-1b9e1321c6bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186351592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186352735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186353467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186353323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186353910 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3828b66d-f82a-5813-9ed6-8d2fc865ed33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186353910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86829" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "520b11ad-97ee-56c3-9607-d0a21f040e1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354518 #edb/ref 1074 "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,3\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{3\\cdot 8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3})≈{19.47}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "664cad5a-9d78-59a1-8bc8-98ba011fc35d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370908 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "196d5cce-e267-5d34-a516-34681744c454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370909 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370909 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "258223e1-67f4-5d69-9403-e0dfa71d0741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370910 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370910 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370910 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46bfc1f1-7af8-5456-b790-9518a6d1e104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370911 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b43d77c-a34b-511a-997b-b60ed018b565" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370912 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370912 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370912 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "624c5226-